 "notes": [
  "Service requests are measured in process from permission-profile resolution through execution and complete response serialization; no HTTP transport is included.",
  "Watched freshness is the daemon's policy (30 s maximum proof age); strict re-walks every visible record per request and is the library default.",
  "The strict restricted metadata read missed its gate (p95 12.87 ms); restricted walks spend about 3.5 ms more than unrestricted ones evaluating grants.",
  "CLI refresh off: p95 33.56 ms (reported separately; not a substitute for the blocking-refresh gate).",
  "Mixed runs use eight readers sharing one session and managed single-record writes at two per second through the real mdbase write path; write latency is the complete plan and apply.",
  "Resident memory grows during mixed runs (for example 154 to 272 MiB over 80K restricted reads at 10K, and about 1 GiB at 100K); whether it levels off is not established by this run.",
  "100K is a scaling case without latency gates. Its restricted mixed reads show a p99 of 497 ms: each write rebuilds the restricted readers' visible link-target index.",
  "Throughput is approximate: samples over whole-run wall time at one-second resolution, including setup.",
  "Cold timings are from fresh copies with a warm OS page cache; the first mdbase query populates the record cache."
